   <text>
      <body>
         <head>To <persName MaryGoldhawkVazeilleWesley="MaryWesley">Mary <addName>(Goldhawk/Vazeille)</addName> Wesley</persName></head>
         <opener>
            <placeName><district>Helston</district></placeName>
            <lb/>
            <date when="1757-09-15">September 15, 1757</date>
            <lb/>
            <lb/>
           </opener>
         <p><index indexName="biblical"><term cRef="Rom12:21">It is a blessed thing to overcome evil with good.<note place="foot" n="1">See Rom. 12:21.</note></term></index> <seg ana="education"><persName you="MaryWesley">You</persName> are at present the mistress of <orgName KingswoodHouse="KingswoodSchool"><placeName><district>Kingswood</district></placeName> house</orgName> and the women there are to follow your direction. If they do not know it, I desire <persName brotherParkinson="JohnParkinson"><addName>brother</addName> Parkinson</persName> to tell them so, <seg ana="mildness">only in a mild and loving manner</seg>. <seg ana="tea moderation">I desire him also to tell them I will allow no one in <orgName thatHouse="KingswoodSchool">that house</orgName> to drink tea twice a day</seg>.</seg></p>
         </body>
      <p><hi rend="italic">Source:</hi> published excerpt, <bibl><hi rend="italic"><persName Wesley="JohnWesley">Wesley</persName>’s Chapel Magazine</hi> 8, no. 30 (<date when="1938-06">June 1938</date>): 11</bibl>.</p>
